From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoxing Hu <hi@xiaoxing.dev>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:36:31 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] embedded: replay a host's output without answering its
 queries

ghostty_surface_write_buffer_replay parses as ghostty_surface_write_buffer
does, and discards at their origin the messages whose only effect is a
reply: the device attributes, cursor and size reports, color and title
reports and clipboard reads. A host that feeds a surface output whose
queries were answered already, by the terminal it came from, does not
want them answered twice.

The flag that discards them is set only while the terminal-state mutex
is held, and every writer that lets go of the mutex clears it for that
while, so that another thread's message is not dropped as replay.

This is what libghostty-spm's Patches/ghostty/0011-replay-response-
suppression.sh at its release 2.2.2026110702 (1d84cf6) does, as a patch:
the script's exact anchors all found, nothing else changed. MIT,
(c) 2026 @Lakr233.
